# ai.wing — build changelog & architecture log

Running log of every significant structural change, feature addition and
architectural decision for the Ting Authorized Retailer landing site.
Newest entries at the bottom.

---

## [0.1.0] — Initial build

### Stack
- Next.js 16.3.5 (App Router, Turbopack) · React 19.2.8 · TypeScript 5
- Tailwind CSS v4 (CSS-first config via `@theme` in `app/globals.css`)
- `lenis` for smooth scrolling
- Static frontend only. No API routes, no database, no server actions.

### Files created
```
lib/content.ts            Single source of truth (plans, copy, disclosures, selectors)
lib/cn.ts                 Class-name joiner
app/globals.css           Ting design tokens + base + reveal animation
app/layout.tsx            Fonts, metadata, skip link, SmoothScroll, SiteHeader
app/page.tsx              Section assembly in canonical order
components/
  SmoothScroll.tsx        Lenis setup + anchor interception
  Reveal.tsx              One-shot IntersectionObserver entrance reveal
  PriceLockup.tsx         Universal <PriceLockup plan={plan} />
  CallButton.tsx          CallButton + PhoneLink (every tel: link routes through here)
  Icons.tsx               Inline SVG icon set
  Wordmark.tsx            Typographic retailer wordmark
  SiteHeader.tsx          Disclosure bar + sticky header + mobile sheet
  ZipChecker.tsx          Client-side ZIP validation → call CTA
  Hero.tsx                Hero with ZIP checker AND call button
  SectionHeading.tsx      Shared eyebrow/heading/subheading
  PlanCard.tsx            Plan card
  ServiceSection.tsx      Generic service-line renderer
  FinePrintGrid.tsx       Comparison table (lg) / stacked cards (<lg)
  WhyUs.tsx               Dark pillars section
  HowItWorks.tsx          Four-step install flow + closing CTA
  Faq.tsx                 Native <details> accordion + FAQPage JSON-LD
  Footer.tsx              Four-column footer + disclosures
.claude/launch.json       Dev server config
```

### Decision — colour palette
Pulled the live CSS custom properties off ting.com rather than guessing. Ting's
published token set:

| Role | Token | Hex |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Primary (blue) | `--primary-60` | `#3253ff` |
| Secondary (coral) | `--secondary-60` | `#ff8c6c` |
| Business dark | `--primary-biz-90` | `#04061e` |
| Greys | `--grey-10` … `--grey-90` | `#f7f7f7` … `#0e0e0e` |

**Note for review:** ting.com paints its own primary buttons *blue* (`#3253ff`).
The brief asked for coral/orange to be dominant, so this build promotes Ting's
official coral secondary (`#ff8c6c`) to the dominant accent and primary CTA, and
keeps the blue as the supporting action colour (ZIP submit). Every hex used is a
real Ting token — nothing invented. The hierarchy is decided in exactly one
place, the semantic aliases in `app/globals.css`:

```css
--color-brand:        var(--color-coral-60);
--color-brand-hover:  var(--color-coral-70);
--color-action:       var(--color-tblue-60);
```

Flipping `--color-brand` to `--color-tblue-60` reverts to ting.com's own
hierarchy without touching a component.

### Decision — contrast
Coral `#ff8c6c` on white with white text is 2.3:1 and fails WCAG AA. All coral
CTAs therefore use near-black `#0e0e0e` text (**8.5:1**). Ting blue with white
text is 5.5:1 and passes as-is.

### Decision — typography
Ting sets Circular Std, which is licensed. Substituted **Figtree** (Google
Fonts) — closest open geometric-humanist sans with the same tall x-height and
tight tracking. Loaded via `next/font/google`, self-hosted, `display: swap`.

### Decision — which service lines exist
Audited ting.com. Ting sells fiber internet and mobile, and nothing else
natively:

| Line | Status | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Fiber | **Included** | Ting Home Fiber $89/mo · Ting Business Fiber (custom pricing) |
| Cable | **Omitted** | Ting is 100% direct fiber. No cable product. |
| Bundle | **Included** | Home Fiber + Unlimited Mobile $99/mo |
| TV | **Omitted** | No native TV product. Legacy TV pages are retired. |
| Mobile | **Included** | Unlimited $25/mo/line · Unlimited Combo $10/mo/line |
| Phone | **Omitted** | Ting Voice is early-release to existing customers only, with no published pricing. A card for it would be exactly the "call to ask" placeholder the brief forbids. |

Omission is data-driven, not hard-coded: `getActiveServiceLines()` filters
`SERVICE_ORDER` down to lines that actually have plans, so adding a TV plan to
`PLANS` makes the TV section appear in the right slot automatically.

### Decision — pricing data (sourced from ting.com)
- Home Fiber: **$89/mo**, 2,000 Mbps symmetrical, unlimited data, no contract
- Bundle: **$99/mo** (vs **$114/mo** separately — $15/mo saving)
- Mobile Unlimited: **$25/mo per line**, $10 off first 3 months
- Mobile Unlimited Combo: **$10/mo per line**, first 3 months free, requires Ting Internet
- Whole Home Wi-Fi+ (eero 7): **from $24/mo**; own router $0; standard install included

### Architecture — the cascade
`lib/content.ts` is the only file carrying a price. Layout files never read the
raw arrays; they consume derived selectors:

- `getLeadPlan()` → hero price anchor
- `getActiveServiceLines()` → which sections render, and in what order
- `getPlansByLine()` → cards inside each section
- `getFinePrintRows()` → every row of the comparison table
- `getNavLinks()` → header nav and anchors
- `getCtaLabel()` → **the CTA text rule lives here, in one place**
- `formatSpeed()` → all speed strings

Changing `price: 89` to `price: 79` updates the hero lockup, the fiber card, the
comparison table and the footer legal line in one edit.

### Architecture — CTA rule
`getCtaLabel(plan)` returns `"Call to order"` when `plan.price` is a number and
`"Call for pricing"` when it is undefined. Cards cannot drift from the rule
because they never author the string themselves.

### Architecture — tel: links
Every `tel:` link renders through `CallButton` or `PhoneLink`, both of which set
`data-call-cta` unconditionally. Verified: 14 tel links, 0 missing the attribute.

### Animation budget
Deliberately small: Lenis smooth scroll (`duration: 1.05`), one-shot fade-and-rise
reveals via IntersectionObserver that unobserve after firing, and CSS hover
transitions on cards and buttons. No WebGL, no 3D, no scroll-linked animation, no
assembly diagrams. All of it collapses under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`,
and a `<noscript>` rule forces `.reveal` visible when JS is unavailable.

### Bug fixed during build
Header call buttons carried `hidden sm:inline-flex`, but `CallButton` bakes
`inline-flex` into its base class string. Both are non-responsive `display`
utilities, so Tailwind's stylesheet order decided the winner and `inline-flex`
won — the "hidden" buttons still occupied layout and pushed the mobile menu
button off-screen at 320px (`body.scrollWidth` 424 vs viewport 320). Fixed by
moving responsive display onto wrapper `<span>`s. Re-verified: `scrollWidth` 320,
0 overflowing elements.

### Verification performed
- `npm run build` — compiles clean, TypeScript passes, `/` prerendered static
- 320px viewport — `document.scrollWidth` 320, **0** overflowing elements
- 14 `tel:` links, **0** missing `data-call-cta`
- Raw phone numbers as link text appear **only** in header (3) and footer (2)
- Plan CTAs read: "Call to order" ×4, "Call for pricing" ×1 (Business Fiber)
- Section order: `top · plans · bundles · mobile · fine-print · why · how-it-works · faq`
- Zero external outbound links; zero broadband/nutrition label links
- Text scan clean for: "pricing observed", "current as of", "last reviewed",
  "county lines", "ordering channel", "network operator", "official site",
  "contact Ting directly", "call to ask"

### Open items for the site owner
1. **Phone number is a placeholder.** `PHONE` in `lib/content.ts` is
   `(888) 555-0100` (reserved fictional range). Replace `display` and `href`.
2. **Footer legal links** point at `#legal`. Swap for real Terms / Privacy /
   Accessibility / Do Not Sell pages when they exist.
3. **Support hours** in `FOOTER_CONTACT` are placeholders.
4. **ZIP checker** validates format only — there is no serviceability API in a
   static build. Wiring a real lookup means replacing the body of `handleSubmit`
   in `components/ZipChecker.tsx`; nothing else needs to change.

