## [0.1.1] — Post-build verification & fixes

### Fixed — speed column fallback
Mobile plans have no `speedDown`, so `getFinePrintRows()` fell back to the
string "Scaled to your needs", which read as nonsense for a wireless plan.
Added an optional `speedLabel` field to `PlanItem` so the label is authored in
data rather than guessed by the formatter:

- `business-fiber` → "Symmetrical, scaled to your business"
- both mobile plans → "Nationwide LTE + 5G"

`formatSpeed()` now returns `plan.speedLabel` when no Mbps figure exists.

### Fixed — unused import
Removed the unused `PHONE` import from `components/Footer.tsx` (lint warning).

### Verified — the cascade actually cascades
Temporarily set the lead plan to `price: 79, cents: '49'` and reloaded. Observed
in a single pass, with no `.tsx` edits:

| Surface | Rendered |
| --- | --- |
| Hero price anchor | `$79.49 per month` |
| Ting Home Fiber card | `$79.49 per month` |
| Comparison table row | `$79.49/mo` |
| Any stale "89" anywhere on the page | none |

Cents handling confirmed too: `.49` surfaces in the table while `.00` is
suppressed. Reverted to `price: 89, cents: '00'`.

### Verified — interaction
- ZIP checker: entering `27587` and submitting renders the confirmation panel
  with its "Call to order" CTA. Non-numeric / short input shows the inline error.
- Mobile menu at 375px: opens, lists Plans · Bundles · Mobile · FAQ + phone,
  closes on selection and on Escape.
- FAQ accordion: native `<details>`, works without JS.
- Sticky header confirmed pinned (`position: sticky`, `rect.top === 0`) while
  Lenis is driving the scroll — no desync.

### Final gate
```
npm run lint    0 errors, 0 warnings
npm run build   compiled clean, TypeScript passed, / prerendered static
```

### Docs
Replaced the default create-next-app README with project documentation covering
the single-source-of-truth workflow, the service-line omission rule, the design
tokens and the pre-launch checklist.

