## [0.3.0] — Professional copy pass, hero call button removed, compact ZIP control

### 1. Copy rewritten for a corporate register

The client flagged seven blocks as reading too casual. Rewritten in
`lib/content.ts` — no `.tsx` edits needed for any of them:

| Section | Before | After |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Hero H1 | "Seriously fast fiber internet / and mobile that stays simple." | "Multi-gig fiber internet / and unlimited mobile." |
| Fiber | "Multi-gig fiber, priced the same every month" | "Dedicated fiber with consistent monthly pricing" |
| Bundle | "Put internet and mobile on one bill" | "Internet and mobile on a single account" |
| Mobile | "Unlimited mobile without the fine print" | "Unlimited mobile on nationwide LTE and 5G" |
| Fine print | "What the monthly number actually covers" | "Plan inclusions and associated costs" |
| Why Ting | "Fiber that behaves the same on a Tuesday night as a Sunday morning" | "Consistent performance at every hour of the day" |
| How it works | "Four steps from call to online" | "From order to installation in four steps" |

Subheadings were rewritten alongside each heading. Folksy constructions removed
throughout: "sold back to you", "the whole street is online", "hold up under
load" (kept, but reframed), "drag your speed down with it", "stop stuttering on
the way out", "promotional cliff at month 13", "bundled in by force".

Also swept for tone consistency, since leaving the bodies casual under
professional headings would have read worse than either:
- All four `WHY_US.pillars` bodies and titles.
- All four `HOW_IT_WORKS.steps` bodies and titles (now noun-phrase labels:
  Address verification · Plan selection · Installation scheduling · Activation).

### 2. Bundle copy no longer hard-codes prices

The bundle subheading quoted "$10 a month instead of $25" as literal text — a
cascade leak, since those two figures also live in `PLANS`. It now interpolates:

```ts
const bundledMobileRate   = PLANS.find(p => p.id === 'mobile-unlimited-combo')?.price;
const standaloneMobileRate = PLANS.find(p => p.id === 'mobile-unlimited')?.price;
// …used in the bundle subheading template literal
```

Changing a mobile price now updates the prose as well as the cards and table.

### 3. Hero call button removed

Removed at the client's explicit second request. **This knowingly departs from
the original brief**, which stated the hero must contain both a ZIP checker and
a call button and that the call button must not be removed. The instruction was
given twice, so it is treated as a deliberate override and is recorded here
rather than silently applied.

Call-to-action coverage after the change:
- Sticky header carries a call button at every breakpoint (on screen throughout).
- All five plan cards carry "Call to order" / "Call for pricing".
- The closing block under How It Works carries "Call to order".
- Hero: ZIP checker only.

To restore it: pass an `action={<CallButton … />}` prop back into `<ZipChecker>`
in `components/Hero.tsx` (the component previously supported this slot).

### 4. ZIP control resized

The availability checker was a full-width white card with a large uppercase
"CHECK AVAILABILITY AT YOUR ADDRESS" header — the client called it oversized.
Rebuilt as a single compact pill:

- Card shell, padding and heading removed; the visual label is gone and the
  `<label>` is now `sr-only`, with the placeholder carrying the instruction.
- Constrained to `max-w-[34rem]` instead of spanning the hero (544px at desktop,
  down from full width).
- Input, search icon and Check button sit in one rounded white pill.
- Helper and result text moved below the pill, styled for the dark hero.
- Measured at 320px: pill 288px, input 158px, **0 overflowing elements**.

### 5. Hero headline set on two lines

The blue accent was stranding a single word ("and") at the end of line one.
Both tones are now `block` spans, so the white and blue halves each own a line.
The accent was also shortened from "and unlimited nationwide mobile." to
"and unlimited mobile.", which brings the lockup from three rendered lines to
two (measured: 64px type, 66px line-height, 1 line per span). "Nationwide"
still appears in the hero subline and the mobile section heading.

### 6. Copyright year removed
`© Ting Authorized Retailer. All rights reserved.` — the `new Date()` call was
dropped with it, so nothing on the page renders a year.

### 7. Section framing moved into content.ts (SSOT gap closed)

Three headings were hard-coded in TSX, outside the single source of truth, and
were also the last casual copy on the page. Moved and rewritten:

| Was hard-coded in | Now |
| --- | --- |
| `Faq.tsx` — "Answers before you pick up the phone" | `FAQ_SECTION` — "Frequently asked questions" |
| `FinePrintGrid.tsx` — "Everything else that can land on the bill" | `FINE_PRINT.addOnsTitle` — "Additional charges that may appear on your bill" |
| `HowItWorks.tsx` — "Ready to find out what your address can get?" | `HOW_IT_WORKS.cta` — "Find out what is available at your address" |

### 8. US spelling
"neighbourhood" → corrected in the FAQ and the Why Ting pillars. No British
spellings remain in `lib/` or `components/`.

### Verification
```
npm run lint    0 errors, 0 warnings
npm run build   compiled clean, TypeScript passed, / prerendered static
```
- 320px — `scrollWidth` 320, **0** overflowing elements
- 11 `tel:` links, **0** missing `data-call-cta`
- Hero: **0** call buttons, ZIP checker present
- Plan CTAs: "Call to order" ×4, "Call for pricing" ×1; closing CTA "Call to order"
- 0 raw phone numbers as link text outside header/footer
- No `© <year>` anywhere; forbidden-phrase scan clean
- Section order unchanged: `top · plans · bundles · mobile · fine-print · why · how-it-works · faq`

