## [0.5.0] — Hero motion, lighter scrim, animated section backgrounds

### 1. The "ghost house" fixed

Two things were draining the photograph: a blue radial glow painted **over** it,
and a scrim that covered the full width at 82–96%. Both gone.

- The blue glow over the image is removed entirely. Ting blue now appears only
  in UI (buttons, eyebrows, the headline accent) and in the drifting aurora
  fields — never as a wash across the photo.
- The scrim is anchored to the left edge and falls to **fully transparent by
  86%** of the width: `from-navy-90 from-6% → via-navy-90/90 via-52% →
  to-transparent to-86%`. The copy sits on near-solid navy; the house keeps its
  own colour.

Contrast was re-measured against the actual pixels after the change, because a
lighter scrim is exactly where legibility breaks:

| Text | Worst case | Needs | |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Headline (large) | 5.44:1 @ 59% across | 3:1 | PASS |
| Subline (normal) | 8.31:1 @ 40% | 4.5:1 | PASS |
| Price label (normal) | 7.68:1 @ 35% | 4.5:1 | PASS |

The spec pills sit past the 86% point where the scrim is gone, so they no longer
rely on it — they carry their own `bg-navy-90/65` backdrop-blurred pill.

### 2. Hero motion

All of it slow and continuous; nothing loops fast enough to pull the eye off the
copy. Defined as `--animate-*` tokens in `@theme`.

- **Ken Burns** on the photograph — 34s, scale 1.02 → 1.12 with a slight drift, alternating.
- **Line reveal** on the headline — each line rises out of its own clipped box,
  staggered 120ms / 260ms. The editorial treatment, not a generic fade.
- **Staggered fade-rise** on eyebrow, subline, price rail, ZIP control and badge
  (460ms → 900ms).
- **Trust marquee** replacing the static chip row — 42s linear, duplicate set for
  a seamless loop (the duplicate is `aria-hidden`), pauses on hover. This mirrors
  the scrolling trust bar on bestfiberinternet.us.
- **Circular badge** floating over the photograph on `xl` and up, carrying
  `HERO.badge` from content.ts. This is the kineticfiber.us device — a real
  element overlapping the image rather than another rectangle in a column.

### 3. Animated gradient fields on the other sections

New `components/Aurora.tsx`: two heavily blurred blobs in Ting blue and coral on
different periods (26s / 32s) so the loop never reads as one. Added to the fiber,
mobile, fine-print, Why Ting, How It Works and FAQ sections. Opacity is 12% on
light sections and 22–30% on dark — it sits under body copy, so it stays well
clear of the contrast budget. The wrapper clips its own overflow, so the
oversized blobs can never widen the page.

### 4. Bundle section uses its photograph as the background

`ServiceSectionMeta` gained `imageTreatment?: 'beside' | 'background'`. The
bundle line is set to `'background'`: the image fills the section behind an 86%
scrim plus a vertical grade, the heading flips to the dark tone and the plan card
sits on top. Still data-driven — any single-plan line can take either treatment.
The image's alt was blanked since it is now decorative.

### 5. Copy and labels
- `Check` → **`Check availability`** (short form retained below `sm`, where the
  full label would not fit the pill).
- Fiber heading → "Fiber-to-the-home internet at a fixed monthly rate"
- Bundle heading → "Internet and mobile consolidated on one account"

### 6. Bugs found and fixed
- **Badge transform conflict.** The circular badge used `-translate-y-1/2` for
  centring while `fade-rise` settles on `transform: none`, which cancelled it and
  dropped the badge half its height. Split: outer element owns the centring, inner
  owns the animation.
- **Hash links did not work on load.** Opening `/#bundles` directly stayed at the
  top — native hash handling runs before Lenis attaches and is then overridden by
  its RAF loop. `SmoothScroll` now re-issues the jump once Lenis owns the scroll
  position. Verified: `/#why` lands with the section 120px from the top, correctly
  clearing the sticky chrome.
- Reduced-motion now switches the looping decoration **off** (`animation: none`)
  rather than compressing it to 0.01ms, which would have left it flickering.

### Verification
```
npm run lint    0 errors, 0 warnings
npm run build   compiled clean, TypeScript passed, / prerendered static
```
- 320px — `scrollWidth` 320, **0 genuinely overflowing elements** (the marquee
  track and Ken Burns image extend past the viewport by design and are clipped by
  their `overflow-hidden` parents; the check now excludes clipped descendants)
- 7 images, 0 broken · 11 `tel:` links, 0 missing `data-call-cta`
- Hero still carries 0 call buttons; plan CTAs unchanged (4 × "Call to order",
  1 × "Call for pricing")
- Animation census: 1 Ken Burns, 12 aurora blobs, 1 marquee, 2 line reveals,
  5 fade-rises
- Forbidden-phrase scan clean; no year stamp; section order unchanged

