## [0.7.0] — Headline contrast bug, hero motion, more vibrant section fields

### 1. "The heading is not highlighted" was a contrast failure, not a taste call

Measured the accent line's colour against the actual pixels behind it. The blue
half of the headline was genuinely washing out:

| Accent colour | Worst case @ 59% across | Large-text floor 3:1 |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `brand-40 #84aeff` (was in use) | **2.45:1** | **FAIL** |
| `aqua #36cec9` | 2.80:1 | FAIL |
| `coral-50 #ffb090` | 3.07:1 | PASS |
| `brand-30 #cfddff` | 4.00:1 | PASS |
| `white #ffffff` | 5.44:1 | PASS |

The scrim falls to nothing by 86% of the width (to keep the house visible), and
the lit windows sit right under the end of the accent line. `#84aeff` simply is
not bright enough to survive that.

Replaced with a gradient fill, every stop of which clears the floor — `#b9d1ff`
(3.52:1) → `#ffffff` (5.43:1) → `#cfddff` (3.99:1) — animated with
`gradient-pan`, so light travels through the line rather than it sitting flat.
Because the gradient pans, *all* stops have to pass, not just the one that
happens to sit at the worst point.

### 2. Headline bloom
A blue radial glow now sits behind the headline on its own slow pulse. It reads
as a highlight and restores the brand colour that moved out of the text.

It also *improves* legibility rather than eroding it: Ting blue has a relative
luminance of 0.14, well below the 0.68 of the lit windows it overlaps, so
compositing it in darkens the worst area of the frame.

### 3. More hero motion
- `gradient-pan` — 9s, light travelling through the accent line.
- `glow-pulse` — 10s, the bloom breathing behind the headline.
- `sheen` — 7s, one pass of light across the price lockup with a long rest
  between passes.
- `float-soft` — 7.5s, the circular badge drifting ±10px.

The badge now nests three elements: positioning (`-translate-y-1/2`), float, and
entrance. All three write to `transform`, so they cannot share an element — the
same class of bug that dropped the badge in 0.5.0.

### 4. Section fields made more vibrant
`Aurora` gained a third blob in Ting's tertiary aqua (`#36cec9`) on a 29s period,
and every blob was pushed up:

| | Blue | Coral | Aqua |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Light sections | 12% → **20%** | 12% → **18%** | — → **14%** |
| Dark sections | 30% → **40%** | 22% → **30%** | — → **22%** |

Three periods (26s / 32s / 29s) share no common multiple inside a session, so
the composite never visibly repeats. Still under body copy, so the ceiling is set
by the text contrast budget rather than by taste.

### Verification
```
npm run lint    0 errors, 0 warnings
npm run build   11 routes, clean
```
- Accent gradient stops: 3.52 / 5.43 / 3.99:1 — all clear the 3:1 large-text floor
- 320px — `scrollWidth` 320, **0 genuinely overflowing elements** (the glow uses
  negative insets but is clipped by the hero's `overflow-hidden`)
- 31 animated elements; all registered in the `prefers-reduced-motion` kill list,
  which switches them off outright rather than compressing them
- DOM check confirms `background-clip: text` resolving and `gradient-pan`,
  `glow-pulse`, `sheen`, `float-soft` all bound

---

## [0.8.0] — Hero entrance choreography

Everything added through 0.7.0 was ambient drift — slow enough to be felt rather
than seen. What was missing was an entrance with a shape to it, and something
that responds to the visitor. Five additions.

### 1. Word-by-word headline reveal
`components/RevealWords.tsx` splits a line into words and staggers them 70ms
apart, each resolving **out of a blur** as it rises (`word-rise`: opacity 0→1,
translateY 0.5em→0, blur 7px→0). Reads as type settling into focus rather than a
generic fade. Six words across two lines, 120ms → 470ms.

**Why the gradient is applied per word, not per line:** `background-clip: text`
clips a background to the glyphs in that element's own paint layer. A descendant
carrying `transform` or `filter` is rasterised separately and drops the fill, so
nesting animated words inside a gradient-filled line renders them invisible.
Keeping clip, transform and blur on the same element sidesteps it — and the
words end up catching the light in sync, which reads as deliberate.

`animation` cannot be declared twice on one element, so the reveal and the
shimmer are composed into a single `--animate-word-shimmer` token.

### 2. Price counts up
`$89` counts from zero on mount with an easeOutExpo curve, 1.1s after a 620ms
delay — it lands just as the chips arrive. Draws the eye to the conversion
anchor.

**This one needed hardening, because it renders a price.** First implementation
was measured showing **`0`**: browsers suspend `requestAnimationFrame` in a
background tab, so the counter reset to zero and never advanced. A visitor
opening the page in a background tab would have seen **$0**. Three guards now:

- SSR renders the real value, so static HTML, no-JS and crawlers get `89`.
- The reset to zero happens in a layout effect, before paint — no flash.
- Animation is skipped entirely under reduced motion **or when
  `document.visibilityState !== 'visible'`**, and a watchdog timer forces the
  final value if the frame loop stalls for any other reason.

Re-verified with the tab hidden: lands on `89`.

### 3. Cursor spotlight
`components/Spotlight.tsx` — a soft light tracking the pointer across the hero.
Writes position to CSS custom properties inside one rAF and lets a
radial-gradient read them, so there is no React state and no re-render per move.
Inert on coarse pointers and under reduced motion; starts transparent and fades
in on first movement so it never appears parked in a corner.

### 4. Border beam on the availability pill
The pill sits inside a 1.5px shell with a conic gradient rotating behind it,
showing through that gap as light running around the border. 5.5s. Draws the eye
to the primary interaction without a colour change or a pulse.

### 5. Spec chips stagger in
`chip-in` on a slight overshoot curve, 90ms apart, timed to land with the price.

### Verification
```
npm run lint    0 errors, 0 warnings
npm run build   11 routes, clean
```
- 6 headline words staggered 0.12s → 0.47s; 3 gradient words resolving
  `word-rise, gradient-pan`; `background-clip: text` confirmed applying
- Price lands on `89` with the tab hidden (the regression case)
- Chips at 0.90 / 0.99 / 1.08s; beam and spotlight both bound
- **38 animated elements**, all in the `prefers-reduced-motion` kill list, which
  now also clears `filter` since `word-rise` animates blur
- 320px — `scrollWidth` 320, **0 genuinely overflowing elements**; the ZIP pill
  gained a wrapper and still fits at 285px with 156px of input

