## [0.9.0] — Four highlight treatments

### 1. Headline
Two layers rather than one. A glyph-hugging `drop-shadow` pair on the `h1` —
a tight dark shadow for separation from the photograph, plus a wide Ting-blue
bloom — and a **marker rule** that wipes out from the left beneath the headline
and then holds the same travelling light as the accent words
(`rule-grow` + `gradient-pan` composed into `--animate-rule-sweep`). The rule
runs blue → coral, which puts the brand colours back on the headline without
putting a low-contrast blue into the type itself.

### 2. Hero background
The hero had no colour field of its own — only the photograph and the scrim.
Added three drifting blobs (blue / aqua / coral) on the existing aurora periods,
**pinned to the left 62% on `lg` and up**.

That constraint is the whole point: the scrim is near-solid over the copy column,
so the blobs read as motion behind the text and never spill onto the house. A
full-width field here would have reproduced exactly the ghosting that the 0.5.0
scrim rework removed.

### 3. "Standard install / Included" badge
Three additions: a halo breathing outward from the disc (`halo`, 6s), a light
running around the rim (the same conic-gradient device as the availability pill),
and a gradient fill with travelling light on the word "Included".

Gradient stops are `#243edb` → `#3253ff` → `#0f1e93` on white, measuring
7.5:1 / 5.5:1 / higher — all clear AA for normal text, never mind the 1.7rem
bold this renders at.

### 4. `$89`
A blue bloom behind the figure, on the same slow pulse as the headline.

Worth noting why this does not cost legibility: Ting blue sits at relative
luminance 0.14, well below anything in the photograph behind it, so compositing
it in **deepens** the backdrop. The white numerals gain contrast rather than
losing it — the same reasoning as the headline bloom in 0.7.0.

### Verification
```
npm run lint    0 errors, 0 warnings
npm run build   11 routes, clean
```
- Marker rule resolving `rule-grow, gradient-pan`, 320px wide at 1440
- Headline carrying both drop-shadows; 2 blooms; 3 hero aurora blobs
- Badge halo bound, rim beam present (2 beams on the page: pill + badge),
  `background-clip: text` applying to the badge value
- **46 animated elements**, all in the `prefers-reduced-motion` kill list
- 320px — `scrollWidth` 320, **0 genuinely overflowing elements**; price still
  lands on `89`

